        "id": 0,
        "original_id": "7b4c8750-f0bb-5908-881c-75f936fb15b4",
        "text": "This chunk is about:\n- People: Richard Connell, Robert Connell, Berthold Viertel, Paul Muni\n- Works: Seven Faces, A Friend of Napoleon, The Saturday Evening Post, The Most Dangerous Game, The Hounds of Zaroff, Collier's, Bloodlust!\n\nFacts:\n- Richard Connell's short fiction \"A Friend of Napoleon\" was published in the June 30, 1923, issue of \"The Saturday Evening Post.\"\n- Richard Connell's short story \"The Most Dangerous Game,\" also published as \"The Hounds of Zaroff,\" was first published in \"Collier's\" on January 19, 1924.\n- \"The Most Dangerous Game\" was Richard Connell's best known work.\n- \"Seven Faces\" was based on Richard Connell's short fiction \"A Friend of Napoleon.\"\n- \"Seven Faces\" was directed by Berthold Viertel.\n- Paul Muni starred in \"Seven Faces\" in his second screen appearance.\n- \"The Most Dangerous Game\" was filmed three years after the 1923 publication of \"A Friend of Napoleon.\"\n- The 1961 American horror thriller film \"Bloodlust!\" was based on Robert Connell's short story \"The Most Dangerous Game.\"",
        "type": "TextSummary"
      },
      {
        "id": 1,
        "original_id": "04edba81-e74d-54cb-89ee-b32ef2009574",
        "text": "Page: Seven Faces. Sentence: Based upon the piece of short fiction \"A Friend of Napoleon\" which was published in the June 30, 1923, issue of \"The Saturday Evening Post\" magazine by popular writer Richard Connell (whose best known work, \"The Most Dangerous Game\", was filmed three years later), it was directed by Berthold Viertel and stars Paul Muni in his second screen appearance.\nPage: The Most Dangerous Game. Sentence: \"The Most Dangerous Game\", also published as \"The Hounds of Zaroff\", is a short story by Richard Connell, first published in \"Collier's\" on January 19, 1924.\nPage: Bloodlust!. Sentence: is a 1961 American horror thriller film based on Robert Connell's short story \"The Most Dangerous Game.\"",
